# Pairs with LogPrefixApplied. The provider before the #5825 fix: a new WAL
# shard activation only reads TAIL on recovery and does not re-stamp it. A
# predecessor on another silo, whose instance commits phase 2 in arrival order,
# still holds a current view of TAIL, so its late commit of a lower batch is not
# fenced: readers of the successor have passed that offset as a settled hole,
# and the entry appears beneath them.
MODULE: LogPrefixAppliedRecoveryLeavesTailUnstamped
TARGET: LogPrefixApplied
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a recovering activation does not re-stamp TAIL, so a predecessor's late lower batch lands beneath readers
PERTURBS: ShardRecover

--- FIND
    \* commit is refused by the fence (issue #5825).
    /\ UNCHANGED ct
    /\ curFresh' = TRUE
    /\ prevFresh' = FALSE
--- REPLACE
    \* commit is refused by the fence (issue #5825).
\* MUTATION: recovery reads TAIL but does not re-stamp it.
    /\ UNCHANGED ct
    /\ curFresh' = TRUE
    /\ UNCHANGED prevFresh
--- END
--- FIND
WithCrossSiloMove == FALSE
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: raises the bound so a lost activation may move to another silo.
WithCrossSiloMove == TRUE
--- END
